#!/usr/bin/python3
"""
encs-switch-tui - terminal UI for the Marvell BobCat2 L2 switch in a Cisco ENCS 5412.

Speaks the same "wcd" XML API that Cisco's switch-confd used, so it needs
neither ConfD nor the (non-functional) embedded web UI.

WHERE TO RUN THIS depends on the hypervisor, because all this needs is an IP
path to 169.254.1.0 over VLAN 2363 on the X710 backplane - never the PCIe
device.

  Proxmox   ON THE HOST. The backplane NIC belongs to the host, so the host
            holds 169.254.1.1 and the bootstrap VM, which only pushes firmware
            over PCIe, cannot reach the switch at all.

  ESXi      IN A VM, and specifically one WITHOUT the Marvell passed through.
            ESXi cannot run this (no bash, no systemd, stripped Python), so a
            guest gets a vNIC on the encs-mgmt-2363 portgroup and 169.254.1.1
            instead. Verified against a live switch from a VM with no PCI
            device at all.

            Do NOT run it in the VM that still has the Marvell attached. That
            VM re-runs the loader at every boot, and a loader run against an
            already-booted ASIC wedges it until AC is pulled. Bootstrap and
            management are separate jobs on this platform; see docs/ESXI.md.

Seven views have a tab and a hotkey (ports, vlans, poe, mac, stats, config,
help); TAB opens a menu with the rest - spanning tree, storm control, port
mirroring, static MACs, LLDP/CDP, LACP tuning, private VLANs, ACLs, QoS,
802.1X, RADIUS, IGMP snooping and L3. Press ? for the full manual.

Environment:
    SW_IP      default 169.254.1.0
    SW_USER    default cisco
    SW_PASS    default cisco
    SW_CFG_DIR default /etc/encs-switch
    ENCS_REPO  GitHub repo --update pulls from
    ENCS_NO_UPDATE_CHECK=1   skip the startup release check entirely
    ENCS_ALLOW_TE_SHUT=1     permit shutting the internal backplane ports
                             (te1-te4). Refused by default - see the manual.

Non-interactive:
    encs-switch-tui --save     capture running config to SW_CFG_DIR
    encs-switch-tui --apply    replay SW_CFG_DIR (used by encs-switch-replay)
    encs-switch-tui --status   one-line health check, exit 0/1
    encs-switch-tui --version  print the version and exit
    encs-switch-tui --check-update   ask GitHub whether a newer release exists
    encs-switch-tui --update   install the latest release (needs root)

Stdlib only.
"""
